IMPORT `ei6-part-9-coming-into-force`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IX: Transitional Provisions (ss 156 to 167). Written by piece ei6
-- (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a person who claimed benefits, or was paid a training allowance, under the old law (the Unemployment Insurance
-- Act, "the former Act", and the National Training Act) and asks which law governs their claim now.
--
-- WHAT THE SECTIONS DO. Sections 156 to 166 say which of two laws governs a matter that was in progress when the
-- former Act was repealed. Pattern 4.1: the answer is a value that names the earlier law, never NOTHING; the day on which
-- the former Act was repealed is s 154's, which the text shows only as [Repeals]; it is read as the day the Act comes
-- into force under s 190(1), June 30, 1996 (assumed, not ruled: fork F-ei6-14 in NOTES.md). The National Training Act's
-- repeal day is not in the text, so a fact about it is a BOOLEAN.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (NOTES.md, coverage table): ss 154 and 155 (placeholders [Repeals]); ss 158, 159(5), 162 and 166
-- (repealed); s 164 (which official exercises a carried-over power, and boards of referees and umpires that continue:
-- machinery); s 167 (power to make transitional regulations); ss 168 to 189 (placeholders [Amendments]).

§ `Repealed provisions`

-- A labelled stub (pattern 9.1): the sections that the text shows only as [Repealed], with nothing for a rule to do.
-- src:3108 | 158 [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2190]
-- src:3125 | (5) [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2191]
-- src:3141 | 162 [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2192]
-- src:3152 | 166 [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2193]
@ref Employment Insurance Act ss 158, 159(5), 162, 166 (src:3108) (src:3125) (src:3141) (src:3152)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`ss 158, 159(5), 162 and 166 - repealed, and therefore not encoded` MEANS
    LIST "158 [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2190]", "(5) [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2191]", "162 [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2192]", "166 [Repealed, 2010, c. 12, s. 2193]"

§ `Sections 156 and 157 - the National Training Act`

-- 156: a training allowance being paid under section 5 of the National Training Act when that Act is repealed may
-- continue to be paid, in accordance with that Act and its regulations as they read immediately before the repeal,
-- until the conclusion of the course to which it relates.
-- src:3105 | 156 A training allowance being paid under section 5 of the National Training Act when it is repealed may continue to be paid in accordance with that Act and the regulations made under it, as they read immediately before the repeal of that Act, until the conclusion of the course to which the allowance relates.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 156 (src:3105)
GIVEN `was being paid under section 5 of the National Training Act when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course to which the allowance relates has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 156 the training allowance may continue to be paid in accordance with the National Training Act` IF
        `was being paid under section 5 of the National Training Act when that Act was repealed`
    AND NOT (`the course to which the allowance relates has concluded`)

-- 157: an agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act in effect when that Act is repealed continues in effect
-- according to its terms.
-- src:3107 | 157 An agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act in effect when it is repealed continues in effect according to the terms of the agreement.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 157 (src:3107)
GIVEN `was an agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act in effect when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 157 the agreement continues in effect according to its terms` IF
    `was an agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act in effect when that Act was repealed`

§ `Section 159 - the Unemployment Insurance Act`

-- The former Act is repealed on the day this Act comes into force (assumed, not ruled: fork F-ei6-14), and the repeal
-- takes effect at the start of that day: a benefit period that begins on that day is not "before" it, and an event on
-- that day is "after" it.
-- src:3112 | 159 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this section, all matters relating to a claim for benefits during a benefit period beginning before the Unemployment Insurance Act (the “former Act”) is repealed shall be dealt with under that Act, including any amendments that may be made by Bill C-31, introduced in the second session of the 35th Parliament and entitled An Act to implement certain provisions of the budget tabled in Parliament on March 6, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1) (src:3112)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 159 the day on which the former Act is repealed` MEANS `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`

-- src:3112 | 159 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this section, all matters relating to a claim for benefits during a benefit period beginning before the Unemployment Insurance Act (the “former Act”) is repealed shall be dealt with under that Act, including any amendments that may be made by Bill C-31, introduced in the second session of the 35th Parliament and entitled An Act to implement certain provisions of the budget tabled in Parliament on March 6, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1) (src:3112)
DECLARE `ei6 Act under which a matter relating to a claim is dealt with` IS ONE OF
    `ei6 the former Act (the Unemployment Insurance Act)`
    `ei6 this Act`

-- (1): except as otherwise provided in section 159, all matters relating to a claim for benefits during a benefit period
-- beginning before the former Act is repealed are dealt with under the former Act. The exceptions are (1.1) to (7) below.
-- src:3112 | 159 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this section, all matters relating to a claim for benefits during a benefit period beginning before the Unemployment Insurance Act (the “former Act”) is repealed shall be dealt with under that Act, including any amendments that may be made by Bill C-31, introduced in the second session of the 35th Parliament and entitled An Act to implement certain provisions of the budget tabled in Parliament on March 6, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1) (src:3112)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `ei6 Act under which a matter relating to a claim is dealt with`
DECIDE `s 159(1) the Act under which matters relating to the claim are dealt with` IS
    IF `the first day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `s 159 the day on which the former Act is repealed`
    THEN `ei6 the former Act (the Unemployment Insurance Act)`
    ELSE `ei6 this Act`

-- (1.01): subsection 70(2) of the former Act applies to appeals under that Act, but the Tax Court of Canada need not give
-- reasons in writing for its decision; it may where it deems that advisable in a particular case.
-- src:3114 | (1.01) Subsection 70(2) of the former Act applies in respect of appeals under that Act except that the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing for its decision but may give reasons in writing where, in a particular case, the Court deems it advisable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1.01) (src:3114)
GIVEN `the appeal is under the former Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing for its decision` IF
    `the appeal is under the former Act`

-- src:3114 | (1.01) Subsection 70(2) of the former Act applies in respect of appeals under that Act except that the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing for its decision but may give reasons in writing where, in a particular case, the Court deems it advisable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1.01) (src:3114)
GIVEN `the appeal is under the former Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada may give reasons in writing for its decision` IF
        `the appeal is under the former Act`
    AND `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing`

-- (1.1): subsection 19(3) applies to claimants who fail to declare earnings in a period determined under the regulations
-- beginning on or after January 5, 1997; the Commission may, on or after that date, make deductions under subparagraph
-- 19(3)(a)(i) for a failure in such a period beginning after June 30, 1996. (Section 190(3.2) says "on or after".)
-- src:3116 | (1.1) Subsection 19(3) of this Act applies to claimants who fail to declare all or some of their earnings in a period determined under the regulations beginning on or after January 5, 1997, but the Commission may make deductions under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i) on or after that date in respect of any failure to declare earnings for such a period beginning after June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1.1) (src:3116)
GIVEN `the first day of the period in which the claimant failed to declare earnings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(1.1) subsection 19(3) applies to the claimant` IF
    `the first day of the period in which the claimant failed to declare earnings` AT LEAST `s 190(3) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (3) come into force`

-- src:3116 | (1.1) Subsection 19(3) of this Act applies to claimants who fail to declare all or some of their earnings in a period determined under the regulations beginning on or after January 5, 1997, but the Commission may make deductions under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i) on or after that date in respect of any failure to declare earnings for such a period beginning after June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1.1) (src:3116)
GIVEN `the day of the deduction` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period in which the claimant failed to declare earnings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(1.1) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` IF
        `the day of the deduction` AT LEAST `s 190(3) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (3) come into force`
    AND `the first day of the period in which the claimant failed to declare earnings` GREATER THAN `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`

-- (1.2): subsection 19(4) applies to claimants who begin attending a course or program after the former Act is repealed.
-- src:3118 | (1.2) Subsection 19(4) of this Act applies to claimants who begin attending a course or program after the former Act is repealed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(1.2) (src:3118)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant begins attending the course or program` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(1.2) subsection 19(4) applies to the claimant` IF
    `the day on which the claimant begins attending the course or program` AT LEAST `s 159 the day on which the former Act is repealed`

-- (2): section 23 applies in place of section 20 of the former Act to claimants claiming benefits for the care of
-- children born or placed for adoption after the former Act is repealed.
-- src:3120 | (2) Section 23 of this Act applies in place of section 20 of the former Act to claimants claiming benefits for the care of children born or placed for adoption after that Act is repealed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(2) (src:3120)
GIVEN `the day on which the child was born or placed for adoption` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(2) section 23 applies in place of section 20 of the former Act` IF
    `the day on which the child was born or placed for adoption` AT LEAST `s 159 the day on which the former Act is repealed`

-- (3), (4): section 25 and section 26 of the former Act apply only to claimants employed on job creation projects, or
-- in a course or program to which they were referred, when the former Act was repealed.
-- src:3122 | (3) Section 25 of the former Act applies only to claimants employed on job creation projects under that section when that Act is repealed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(3) (src:3122)
GIVEN `was employed on a job creation project under section 25 of the former Act when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(3) section 25 of the former Act applies to the claimant` IF
    `was employed on a job creation project under section 25 of the former Act when that Act was repealed`

-- src:3124 | (4) Section 26 of the former Act applies only to claimants in a course or program to which they are referred under that section before that Act is repealed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(4) (src:3124)
GIVEN `was in a course or program to which the claimant was referred under section 26 of the former Act before that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(4) section 26 of the former Act applies to the claimant` IF
    `was in a course or program to which the claimant was referred under section 26 of the former Act before that Act was repealed`

-- (6): sections 27 to 33 of this Act apply in place of sections 27 to 28.3 of the former Act for events occurring after
-- the former Act is repealed that give rise to a disentitlement or disqualification; and a reference in the former Act
-- to section 27, 28, 28.1, 28.2 or 28.3 is read as a reference to section 27, 29, 31, 32 or 33 of this Act.
-- src:3127 | (6) Sections 27 to 33 of this Act apply in place of sections 27 to 28.3 of the former Act in respect of events occurring after that Act is repealed that give rise to a disentitlement or disqualification under those sections and, for the purpose of applying those sections, a reference in the former Act to
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(6) (src:3127)
GIVEN `the day of the event giving rise to the disentitlement or disqualification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(6) sections 27 to 33 apply in place of sections 27 to 28.3 of the former Act` IF
    `the day of the event giving rise to the disentitlement or disqualification` AT LEAST `s 159 the day on which the former Act is repealed`

-- src:3128 | (a) section 27 shall be read as a reference to section 27 of this Act;
-- src:3129 | (b) section 28 shall be read as a reference to section 29 of this Act;
-- src:3130 | (c) section 28.1 shall be read as a reference to section 31 of this Act;
-- src:3131 | (d) section 28.2 shall be read as a reference to section 32 of this Act; and
-- src:3132 | (e) section 28.3 shall be read as a reference to section 33 of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(6) (src:3128-3132)
GIVEN `the number of the section of the former Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` IS
    BRANCH IF `the number of the section of the former Act` EQUALS 27   THEN JUST 27
           IF `the number of the section of the former Act` EQUALS 28   THEN JUST 29
           IF `the number of the section of the former Act` EQUALS 28.1 THEN JUST 31
           IF `the number of the section of the former Act` EQUALS 28.2 THEN JUST 32
           IF `the number of the section of the former Act` EQUALS 28.3 THEN JUST 33
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (7): section 145 of this Act applies in place of section 123 of the former Act for benefits paid after December 31, 1995.
-- src:3134 | (7) Section 145 of this Act applies in place of section 123 of the former Act in respect of benefits paid after December 31, 1995.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 159(7) (src:3134)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefits were paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 159(7) section 145 applies in place of section 123 of the former Act` IF
    `the day on which the benefits were paid` GREATER THAN (YMD 1995 12 31)

§ `Sections 160 and 161 - hours, earnings and premiums before 1997`

-- 160: for calculating after 1996 how many hours of insurable employment and what insurable earnings a claimant has under
-- this Act, other than Part VIII, those before June 30, 1996 are determined under the former Act, and those on or after
-- June 30, 1996 but before January 5, 1997 under this Act as it applies on June 30, 1996. The section says nothing of
-- hours and earnings from January 5, 1997 or of Part VIII: NOTHING.
-- src:3136 | 160 For the purpose of calculating after 1996 how many hours of insurable employment and the amount of insurable earnings a claimant has under this Act, other than Part VIII, insurable employment and insurable earnings occurring
-- src:3137 | (a) before June 30, 1996 shall be determined in accordance with the former Act; and
-- src:3138 | (b) on or after June 30, 1996 but before January 5, 1997 shall be determined in accordance with this Act, as it applies on June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 160 (src:3136-3138)
DECLARE `ei6 Law that determines insurable employment and insurable earnings before 1997` IS ONE OF
    `ei6 the former Act`
    `ei6 this Act as it applies on June 30, 1996`

-- src:3136 | 160 For the purpose of calculating after 1996 how many hours of insurable employment and the amount of insurable earnings a claimant has under this Act, other than Part VIII, insurable employment and insurable earnings occurring
-- src:3137 | (a) before June 30, 1996 shall be determined in accordance with the former Act; and
-- src:3138 | (b) on or after June 30, 1996 but before January 5, 1997 shall be determined in accordance with this Act, as it applies on June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 160 (src:3136-3138)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefits are claimed` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the day on which the insurable employment and insurable earnings occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei6 Law that determines insurable employment and insurable earnings before 1997`
DECIDE `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` IS
    BRANCH IF `the Part under which the benefits are claimed` EQUALS `Part VIII` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the day on which the insurable employment and insurable earnings occurred` LESS THAN `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force` THEN JUST `ei6 the former Act`
           IF `the day on which the insurable employment and insurable earnings occurred` LESS THAN `s 190(3) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (3) come into force` THEN JUST `ei6 this Act as it applies on June 30, 1996`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 161: all matters relating to the payment of premiums under the former Act are dealt with under that Act.
-- src:3140 | 161 All matters relating to the payment of premiums under the former Act shall be dealt with under that Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 161 (src:3140)
GIVEN `the matter relates to the payment of premiums under the former Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 161 the matter is dealt with under the former Act` IF
    `the matter relates to the payment of premiums under the former Act`

§ `Section 163 - estimated insurable earnings and plan for 1996-97`

-- Duties of the Commission toward the public, not of the person: no seat question. Each estimate or plan is published in
-- the Canada Gazette if it is not set out in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for 1996-97.
-- src:3143 | 163 (1) For the purposes of section 78, the Commission’s estimate of the insurable earnings of all insured persons in the fiscal year 1996-97 shall be published in the Canada Gazette if it is not set out in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for that year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 163(1) (src:3143)
GIVEN `the estimate is set out in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for 1996-97` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 163(1) the Commission's estimate of the insurable earnings of all insured persons in the fiscal year 1996-97 must be published in the Canada Gazette` IF
    NOT (`the estimate is set out in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for 1996-97`)

-- src:3145 | (2) The plan mentioned in section 79 shall be published in the Canada Gazette for the fiscal year 1996-97 if it is not included in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for that year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 163(2) (src:3145)
GIVEN `the plan is included in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for 1996-97` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 163(2) the plan mentioned in section 79 for the fiscal year 1996-97 must be published in the Canada Gazette` IF
    NOT (`the plan is included in the Main Estimates tabled in Parliament for 1996-97`)

§ `Section 165 - waivers and agreements`

-- 165: waivers and agreements made under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the former Act and in effect when that Act is repealed
-- continue in effect as though they had been made under paragraph 5(4)(d) of this Act.
-- src:3151 | 165 Waivers and agreements made under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the former Act and in effect when that Act is repealed continue in effect as though they had been made under paragraph 5(4)(d) of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 165 (src:3151)
GIVEN `was a waiver or agreement made under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the former Act and in effect when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 165 the waiver or agreement continues in effect as though made under paragraph 5(4)(d) of this Act` IF
    `was a waiver or agreement made under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the former Act and in effect when that Act was repealed`
